.TH JAVASPEC 1 "July 2026" "javaspec" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
javaspec \- subject-centric SpecBDD for Java inspired by PHPSpec
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B javaspec describe
.I ClassName
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B javaspec desc
.I ClassName
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B javaspec run
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B javaspec prophesize
.I FQCN
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B javaspec list-extensions
.br
.B javaspec
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B javaspec
is a PHPSpec-inspired, subject-centric specification tool for Java. Specifications use public
.B it_*
or
.B its_*
examples, lifecycle methods such as
.B let
and
.BR letGo ,
construction helpers,
.B subject(),
and fluent
.B should*
expectations.
.PP
The core runs on Java 8 and has no third-party runtime dependencies. Optional Maven, Gradle, JUnit Platform, bytecode-doubles, and bytecode-agent adapters are distributed separately.
.PP
.B describe
creates specification and generated support skeletons only. It never creates production code.
.B run
discovers specifications, plans or applies authorized generation, optionally compiles sources, executes examples, and writes reports.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B describe, desc
Create a PHPSpec-style specification skeleton for
.IR ClassName .
The
.B desc
form is an alias.
.TP
.B run
Discover and execute specifications. Generation writes require an affirmative prompt or
.BR \-\-generate .
.TP
.B prophesize
Generate a typed
.B *Prophecy
wrapper for an interface or concrete class.
.TP
.B list-extensions
List built-in and ServiceLoader-discovered formatters and extensions, followed by classpath repair hints.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Load the line-based javaspec configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-suite " name"
Select a configured suite.
.TP
.BI \-\-spec-dir " dir"
Use the given specification source root. The default is
.BR src/test/java .
.B \-\-spec-root
is an alias.
.SH RUN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-source-dir " dir"
Use the given production source root. The default is
.BR src/main/java .
.B \-\-source-root
is an alias.
.TP
.BI \-\-classpath " paths"
Add explicit classpath entries separated by the platform path separator.
.TP
.BI \-\-classpath-file " file"
Read UTF-8 classpath entries, one per non-empty, non-comment line.
.TP
.BI \-\-resolve-pom " pom.xml"
Resolve runtime dependencies from the local Maven repository or a configured dependency resolver.
.TP
.B \-\-compile
Compile production and specification source trees before execution.
.TP
.BI \-\-compile-output " dir"
Write compiled classes to
.IR dir ;
implies
.BR \-\-compile .
The default is
.BR target/javaspec-classes .
.TP
.BI \-\-release " N"
Compile for Java release
.IR N .
Requires compilation.
.TP
.B \-\-generate
Authorize non-interactive production and generated-support writes.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Plan generation and updates without writing, prompting, or compiling.
.TP
.B \-\-stop-on-failure
Stop after the first failed or broken executable example.
.TP
.BR \-\-auto-check-predictions , " " \-\-no-auto-check-predictions
Enable or disable automatic Prophecy prediction verification. It is enabled by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-formatter " name"
Select
.BR progress ,
.BR pretty ,
.BR json ,
or a discovered formatter. JSON reserves standard output for one JSON document.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " profile"
Select
.BR java8 ,
.BR java11 ,
.BR java17 ,
.BR java21 ,
or
.BR java25 .
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print the effective run configuration before discovery.
.TP
.BI \-\-report " file"
Write a UTF-8 JSON example-run report.
.B \-\-report-file
is an alias.
.TP
.BI \-\-generation-report " file"
Always write a deterministic UTF-8 generation outcome report, including dry-run and failed pipelines.
.TP
.BI \-\-junit-xml " file"
Write a UTF-8 JUnit XML-compatible report.
.B \-\-junit-xml-file
is an alias.
.TP
.BI \-\-constructor-policy " policy"
Choose
.BR delete ,
.BR preserve ,
or
.BR comment .
The default is
.BR comment .
.TP
.BI \-\-class " name"
Filter by described or specification class. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-example " name"
Filter by example method, display name, or source-order index. Repeatable.
.SH PROPHESIZE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-output " dir"
Generated wrapper destination. The default is
.BR target/generated-sources/javaspec .
.TP
.BI \-\-package " name"
Set the generated wrapper package.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Replace an existing generated wrapper.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print generated source without writing it.
.SH GENERATION SAFETY
Generation is mechanical and fail-closed. Production writes require explicit authorization and are atomic where the filesystem supports it. Generated method bodies contain a
.B // javaspec:stub
marker; a compiled run remains BROKEN until those stubs are implemented. Ambiguous source or type evidence is refused before writes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful run, including skipped-only or pending-only examples when no generation work remains.
.TP
.B 1
Failed or broken examples, declined or pending generation work, or compilation failure.
.TP
.B 64
Usage, profile, compiler availability, bootstrap, or compatibility error.
.TP
.B 70
Input/output or security-related file error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B src/test/java
Default specification root.
.TP
.B src/main/java
Default production source root.
.TP
.B target/generated-sources/javaspec
Default generated support and Prophecy wrapper root.
.TP
.B target/javaspec-classes
Default CLI compilation output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a specification, generate missing mechanical scaffolding, compile, and run:
.PP
.nf
javaspec describe com.example.PriceCalculator
javaspec run --generate --compile --formatter pretty
.fi
.PP
Check generation without changing the workspace:
.PP
.nf
javaspec run --dry-run \
  --generation-report target/javaspec-generation.json
.fi
.PP
Run one example under the Java 21 profile:
.PP
.nf
javaspec run --profile java21 --class PriceCalculator \
  --example it_calculates_total --compile
.fi
